{
  "name": "wall_crouch_idle",
  "note": "(anim-rework S5 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) Back to the wall, crouched: CT's side-on crouch (the game turns the body 83 deg toward the open side, WALL_SIDE; this clip is in that posed frame, the wall on the LEFT, the open side ahead; mirrored for the other side): a deep balanced squat as the crouched idle (knees 112 deg, feet hip width and flat, the hips about 37 cm down and 10 cm behind the feet), the trunk about 45 deg over the knees (pelvis 24, chest 42), the head up looking ahead; the open-side (right) hand rests on top of its knee, palm down and fingers forward (wrist frame on every key; the game's KNEE_HAND keeps the contact), the wall-side (left) hand hangs low by its shin. Alive: three slow breaths, a weight shift, a slow look ahead and back toward the wall. Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward; wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Holstered arms; with a weapon drawn the arms stay procedural. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
